-- 4. Rotational cryptanalysis -------------------------------
   ARX ciphers can respect rotations: Pr[E(x<<<r) = E(x)<<<r] should
   be 2^-96, and modular addition alone preserves rotations with
   probability (1 + 2^-r + ...)/4 per operation, so constants matter
